1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:03,921
Coming up.

2
00:00:03,921 --> 00:00:08,097
Over the Continental Divide at 11,312 feet.

3
00:00:08,097 --> 00:00:11,302
Colorado's largest body of water.

4
00:00:11,302 --> 00:00:16,547
And a hot-springs town walled in by 13,000-foot peaks.

5
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:23,899
Denver to Ouray: 305 miles, 6 stops, and 2 mountain passes over 10,000 feet.

6
00:00:23,899 --> 00:00:28,112
Stick around to the end for the full trip planner.

7
00:00:29,062 --> 00:00:30,211
Here's the plan.

8
00:00:30,211 --> 00:00:38,184
We leave Denver, stop at Kenosha Pass, Buena Vista, Monarch Pass, and Blue Mesa Reservoir, and finish in Ouray.

9
00:00:39,134 --> 00:00:47,363
We start in Denver, exactly one mile high, and point the car southwest on US 285.

10
00:00:47,363 --> 00:00:52,848
The 13th step of the State Capitol sits at 5,280 feet.

11
00:00:52,848 --> 00:00:55,795
Look for the engraved marker.

12
00:00:56,745 --> 00:01:02,271
US 285 climbs out of the foothills, through Conifer and Bailey, toward the Divide.

13
00:01:02,271 --> 00:01:08,404
Bailey sits on the North Fork of the South Platte, the same river that runs through Denver.

14
00:01:09,354 --> 00:01:15,598
Kenosha Pass tops out at 10,001 feet, and the whole of South Park opens up below.

15
00:01:15,598 --> 00:01:18,989
In late September the aspens here turn gold.

16
00:01:18,989 --> 00:01:23,306
It's one of the busiest leaf-peeping spots in the state.

17
00:01:24,256 --> 00:01:30,228
Across South Park and over Trout Creek Pass, the Collegiate Peaks fill the windshield.

18
00:01:30,228 --> 00:01:34,811
Fairplay is one of the towns that inspired the cartoon South Park.

19
00:01:35,761 --> 00:01:40,847
Buena Vista sits under a wall of fourteeners on the Arkansas River.

20
00:01:40,847 --> 00:01:48,058
Mount Princeton, Yale, Harvard and Columbia are all over 14,000 feet and all visible from town.

21
00:01:49,008 --> 00:01:55,517
South to Poncha Springs, then US 50 climbs hard toward the Continental Divide.

22
00:01:55,517 --> 00:02:01,108
From Poncha Springs, US 50 gains over 3,800 feet in about 18 miles.

23
00:02:02,058 --> 00:02:04,362
Monarch Pass: 11,312 feet.

24
00:02:04,362 --> 00:02:08,527
Rain that falls here splits between two oceans.

25
00:02:08,527 --> 00:02:13,135
Water on the east side drains to the Gulf of Mexico.

26
00:02:13,135 --> 00:02:16,326
The west side drains to the Pacific.

27
00:02:17,276 --> 00:02:22,451
Down the west side through Gunnison, then along the shore of Blue Mesa.

28
00:02:22,451 --> 00:02:27,044
Gunnison is one of the coldest towns in the lower 48 in winter.

29
00:02:27,994 --> 00:02:33,284
Blue Mesa is the largest body of water entirely inside Colorado.

30
00:02:33,284 --> 00:02:37,417
It's the biggest kokanee salmon fishery in the US.

31
00:02:37,417 --> 00:02:40,228
Its shoreline runs about 96 miles.

32
00:02:41,178 --> 00:02:47,172
Over Cerro Summit to Montrose, then south on US 550 into the San Juans.

33
00:02:47,172 --> 00:02:52,913
The Black Canyon of the Gunnison is a short detour east of Montrose.

34
00:02:52,913 --> 00:02:55,952
Its Painted Wall is 2,250 feet tall.

35
00:02:56,902 --> 00:02:59,802
Ouray, boxed in by 13,000-foot peaks.

36
00:02:59,802 --> 00:03:01,683
Soak in the hot springs.

37
00:03:01,683 --> 00:03:02,781
You earned it.

38
00:03:02,781 --> 00:03:11,402
Ouray calls itself the Switzerland of America, and the Million Dollar Highway starts at the south end of town.

39
00:03:12,352 --> 00:03:21,184
That's 305 miles from Denver to Ouray, topping out at 11,312 feet near Monarch Pass.

40
00:03:22,134 --> 00:03:25,104
Here's everything you need to plan it yourself.

41
00:03:25,104 --> 00:03:27,000
Pause and screenshot this one.

42
00:03:30,634 --> 00:03:32,043
Thanks for riding along.

43
00:03:32,043 --> 00:03:36,623
Subscribe for more road trips, and I'll see you on The Million Dollar Highway.
